    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1733">

                <pb facs="1401" n="1285" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.124/42.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to enclose herewith, for
                    transmission to the President of Peru, the letter of acceptance of Mr.
                    Bayless.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bayless informs the Department that a Mr. Keegan, one of the assistants in
                    the Health Department of the city of Richmond, Virginia, has agreed to join him
                    at Iquitos, sailing on November 15, and Mr. Keegan’s letter of acceptance will
                    be forwarded later.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
